# 8. Error Handling

Sabhi modifying tools (`add_gate`, `remove_gate`, `clear_circuit`, `delete_circuit`) `try/catch` ke through errors handle karte hain.

Example:

```js
catch (error) {
  return {
    content: [
      {
        type: "text",
        text: `Error: ${error.message}`,
      },
    ],
    isError: true,
  };
}
```

Agar operation fail hota hai, MCP client ko `isError: true` ke saath error response milta hai.

Isse client ko pata chal sakta hai ki operation successfully execute nahi hua.

---

# 9. Input Validation

MCP tools ke parameters ko validate karne ke liye **Zod** use kiya gaya hai.

Example:

```js
gate: z.enum(["H", "X", "Y", "Z", "S", "T"])
```

Iska matlab sirf supported gates accept honge.

Similarly:

```js
qubit: z.number().int().min(0)
```

ensure karta hai ki qubit ek non-negative integer ho.

Input validation invalid requests ko server ke business logic tak pahunchne se pehle reject karne me help karti hai.

---

# 10. MCP Transport

Server `StdioServerTransport` use karta hai:

```js
const transport = new StdioServerTransport();

await server.connect(transport);
```

Iska purpose MCP client aur server ke beech communication establish karna hai.

Server tools ko MCP protocol ke through client ke liye available kar deta hai.

---

# 11. CircuitService Integration

`server.js` me actual circuit manipulation logic directly nahi likha gaya hai.

Instead, server `CircuitService` ko use karta hai:

```text
MCP Tool
   ↓
CircuitService
   ↓
Circuit Map
```

Example:

```text
AI / MCP Client
       ↓
    add_gate
       ↓
circuitService.addGate()
       ↓
   Circuit updated
```

Is separation se MCP tool layer aur circuit business logic independent rehte hain.

